      "metadata": {
        "title": "White Line: A Typed Ledger for the Edge of the Claim",
        "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24124429",
        "publication_date": "2026-11-11",
        "description": "<p>A typed ledger for absence: epistemic gaps, ethical restraint, and contemplative negative space. It records what is missing, withheld, or unresolved under a total caution order, decays stale namings past their review horizons, and refuses to infer why anything is absent. Withholding is recorded as a boundary, never mined as missing evidence.</p><p><strong>Subtitle:</strong> Keeping missing evidence, ethical boundaries, and open questions from becoming unsupported claims</p><p>Code is MIT licensed; prose and figures are CC BY 4.0. See LICENSE in the repository.</p>",
