        "notes": "White Line is a peer instrument whose current membership belongs to https://github.com/docxology/line_set; the original four were Red, Black, Golden, and White. The colorless reader and Witness Register are not colors. Copper resource accounting does not quantify White gaps or prove fair allocation; missing recovery evidence can be White absence, while Iron recorded recovery target comparisons do not promise future recovery. Violet, Copper, and Iron sources are access-controlled. Five existing sibling DOI relationships are retained historical identities, not an exhaustive inventory. Membership is not source access. Previously verified source archive: 0.9.1, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24069434; identifies that source ZIP only, not a standalone manuscript. DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21754242 remains an earlier historical archive reference. This metadata cites later source through its repository until that exact edition/object is independently verified."
